1
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:20,640
<i>A hundred years ago, in one night, the sea left.</i>

2
00:00:36,250 --> 00:00:39,400
<i>The law says every light burns till dawn.</i>

3
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:43,560
<i>Nobody remembers why.</i>

4
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:49,600
[Orla] You climb like the stairs owe you money.

5
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,040
[Espen] You ring like the bell owes you dinner.

6
00:01:53,220 --> 00:01:56,980
[Orla] Two rings means food. You came up on one and a half.

7
00:01:57,585 --> 00:02:01,735
[Espen] Found a whole vein of blue under the third rib. Look at it.

8
00:02:01,915 --> 00:02:04,135
[Orla] Mm. The sea's old teeth.

9
00:02:04,730 --> 00:02:07,170
[Espen] It's salt with a mood, Gran.

10
00:02:07,350 --> 00:02:10,830
[Orla] Everything down there is something with a mood.

11
00:02:16,435 --> 00:02:18,035
[Espen] I had it.

12
00:02:18,435 --> 00:02:21,755
[Orla] You had the floor. The floor had the kettle.

13
00:02:21,935 --> 00:02:23,715
[Espen] Your hands okay?

14
00:02:24,315 --> 00:02:28,025
[Orla] My hands are seventy. Ask them nothing before noon.

15
00:02:37,815 --> 00:02:41,135
[Espen] Hulda's caravan goes out after storm season.

16
00:02:41,315 --> 00:02:45,125
[Orla] So does every fool with two legs and no roof to mind.

17
00:02:45,730 --> 00:02:49,880
[Espen] If I sell the whole jar, I can get the wheel. The good one.

18
00:02:50,060 --> 00:02:51,660
[Espen] With spokes.

19
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:53,440
[Orla] Oil first.

20
00:02:54,035 --> 00:02:57,575
[Espen] It's always oil first. We eat oil. We dream oil.

21
00:02:57,755 --> 00:03:01,135
[Orla] When you keep a lamp, you'll count different.

22
00:03:01,730 --> 00:03:05,050
[Espen] I don't keep a lamp. I carry stairs for one.

23
00:03:05,230 --> 00:03:09,650
[Orla] Then carry the can to Hulda's. Full weight, and watch her thumb.

24
00:03:10,250 --> 00:03:12,470
[Espen] Her thumb weighs a fish.

25
00:03:12,750 --> 00:03:14,750
[Orla] So does your excuse.

26
00:03:36,250 --> 00:03:40,450
[Hulda] Kelp glass, bone buttons... and what is this, a saint's toe?

27
00:03:40,630 --> 00:03:44,340
[Espen] Whale ear-stone. Worth your whole awning, probably.

28
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:47,350
[Hulda] Probably. The word I pay least for.

29
00:03:48,440 --> 00:03:50,940
[Hulda] Oil's up again. Storm season.

30
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:54,390
[Hulda] Everything true costs more in storm season.

31
00:03:55,940 --> 00:03:58,050
[Espen] Gran says full weight.

32
00:03:58,230 --> 00:04:01,770
[Hulda] Your gran says a lot of hundred-year-old things.

33
00:04:02,370 --> 00:04:06,350
[Hulda] A century, boy. Not one ship. Not a rowboat. Not a duck.

34
00:04:06,530 --> 00:04:09,850
[Hulda] And she burns coin every night to warn them.

35
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:12,350
[Espen] Yeah.

36
00:04:13,750 --> 00:04:15,350
[Hulda] Yeah?

37
00:04:16,550 --> 00:04:19,260
[Espen] It's a museum. She's the exhibit.

38
00:04:21,450 --> 00:04:26,250
[Hulda] Ha! Ten years I've said it. First time a keeper's blood agreed with me.

39
00:04:27,450 --> 00:04:29,840
[Espen] Apprentice. It's different.

40
00:04:30,020 --> 00:04:32,410
[Hulda] Not in the ledger it isn't.

41
00:04:34,950 --> 00:04:39,370
[Hulda] Spring caravan. There's still a place, if your legs are serious.

42
00:04:42,450 --> 00:04:44,340
[Espen] I asked, didn't I?

43
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:48,770
[Hulda] You asked like a boy buying something behind his gran's back.

44
00:04:48,950 --> 00:04:50,560
[Espen] It's my back.

45
00:04:53,450 --> 00:04:56,550
[Hulda] Funny. Can't see Farholm's tower lately.

46
00:04:59,550 --> 00:05:01,150
[Espen] It's noon.

47
00:05:01,950 --> 00:05:05,160
[Hulda] At noon you see the tower. Haze, probably.

48
00:05:13,450 --> 00:05:15,050
[Espen] Cheap junk.

49
00:05:35,450 --> 00:05:37,050
[Orla] Hands.

50
00:05:39,150 --> 00:05:42,800
[Orla] Softer than mine were at eight. Never mind. Watch.

51
00:05:46,750 --> 00:05:51,170
[Orla] Minute one: shut the pane. Wind is a thief with patient fingers.

52
00:05:53,450 --> 00:05:55,230
[Espen] The pane's fine.

53
00:05:55,950 --> 00:05:59,430
[Orla] The pane is cracked and you've been told twice.

54
00:05:59,610 --> 00:06:02,270
[Espen] It whistles. I like the whistle.

55
00:06:03,175 --> 00:06:06,765
[Orla] Minute two: trim the wick. Black beard, no flame.

56
00:06:10,175 --> 00:06:14,265
[Orla] Minute three: oil to the ring. Not past it, not shy of it.

57
00:06:16,975 --> 00:06:20,295
[Orla] Minute four: dry hands, dry matches. Say it.

58
00:06:21,175 --> 00:06:23,345
[Espen] Dry hands, dry matches.

59
00:06:24,975 --> 00:06:27,145
[Orla] Say it like it's yours.

60
00:06:27,975 --> 00:06:30,145
[Espen] Dry hands. Dry matches.

61
00:06:31,475 --> 00:06:34,575
[Orla] Minute five: strike away from your body.

62
00:06:36,575 --> 00:06:38,405
[Orla] Minute six: burn.

63
00:06:41,675 --> 00:06:43,565
[Espen] And if it doesn't?

64
00:06:45,455 --> 00:06:48,285
[Espen] Gran. What happens at minute seven?

65
00:06:49,975 --> 00:06:53,015
[Orla] The tin holds eight. Buy more tomorrow.

66
00:06:54,975 --> 00:06:59,455
[Orla] Matches sleep on the stove ledge. Every night. Even when I don't.

67
00:07:02,975 --> 00:07:05,965
[Espen] Six minutes. It's a lamp, not a heart.

68
00:07:17,875 --> 00:07:20,865
[Orla] Behind the great lens. One spare. Dry.

69
00:07:22,075 --> 00:07:24,625
[Espen] Ow— fine. One spare. For what?

70
00:07:26,575 --> 00:07:29,345
[Orla] For the night the tin lies to you.

71
00:07:40,075 --> 00:07:43,015
[Espen] I told Hulda yes. The spring caravan.

72
00:07:44,375 --> 00:07:46,975
[Espen] ...You're supposed to yell now.

73
00:07:48,175 --> 00:07:51,215
[Orla] Am I? Whose lungs are you volunteering?

74
00:07:54,075 --> 00:07:57,665
[Orla] Then sign out properly when you go. Keepers sign.

75
00:08:00,175 --> 00:08:02,005
[Espen] I'm not a keeper.

76
00:08:03,175 --> 00:08:06,115
[Orla] Everyone in that book said that once.

77
00:08:13,875 --> 00:08:16,205
[Espen] This name's spelled wrong.

78
00:08:16,875 --> 00:08:20,465
[Orla] Your great-great-uncle. Spelled everything wrong.

79
00:08:20,645 --> 00:08:22,865
[Orla] Kept forty years anyway.

80
00:08:23,570 --> 00:08:25,570
[Espen] Forty years of this?

81
00:08:25,750 --> 00:08:29,560
[Orla] Forty years of dawns. You only ever count the nights.

82
00:08:30,665 --> 00:08:33,105
[Espen] The storm looks like a wall.

83
00:08:33,865 --> 00:08:36,905
[Orla] It is a wall. Ours just burns brighter.

84
00:08:37,765 --> 00:08:40,155
[Espen] That doesn't mean anything.

85
00:08:40,365 --> 00:08:43,305
[Orla] Most true things don't. Till they do.

86
00:08:44,665 --> 00:08:48,205
[Orla] Eat. If the wind takes you, I want it to strain.

87
00:09:03,665 --> 00:09:06,815
[Orla] Bed. If the bell rings, it rings for you.

88
00:09:07,665 --> 00:09:09,885
[Espen] It never rings at night.

89
00:09:12,165 --> 00:09:14,055
[Orla] No. It never does.

90
00:09:30,665 --> 00:09:33,215
<i>[signal bell — dragged, wrong]</i>

91
00:09:46,165 --> 00:09:47,765
[Espen] Gran? Gran—

92
00:10:02,465 --> 00:10:04,575
[Espen] Okay. Up. Come on, up—

93
00:10:05,665 --> 00:10:08,655
[Espen] —why are you heavy, you weigh nothing—

94
00:10:21,465 --> 00:10:23,065
[Orla] Pane.

95
00:10:24,165 --> 00:10:27,875
[Espen] I know. I know, I'm sorry, I'll fix it, just stand—

96
00:10:28,165 --> 00:10:29,765
[Orla] Light first.

97
00:10:30,565 --> 00:10:32,565
[Espen] You're on the floor!

98
00:10:34,365 --> 00:10:35,965
[Orla] Then me.

99
00:10:37,765 --> 00:10:39,365
[Espen] Gran—

100
00:10:39,765 --> 00:10:41,365
[Orla] Count.

101
00:10:43,665 --> 00:10:45,265
[Orla] Count.

102
00:11:06,665 --> 00:11:08,995
[Espen] Minute one. Shut the pane.

103
00:11:24,665 --> 00:11:26,995
[Espen] Minute two. Trim the wick.

104
00:11:33,665 --> 00:11:36,215
[Espen] Minute three. Oil to the ring.

105
00:11:41,165 --> 00:11:43,605
[Espen] Minute four. Dry hands. Dry—

106
00:11:49,665 --> 00:11:51,775
[Espen] No. No no no. Not now—

107
00:12:09,965 --> 00:12:13,065
[Espen] Minute five. Strike away from your body.

108
00:12:16,165 --> 00:12:19,105
[Espen] That was still five. It's still five!

109
00:13:00,165 --> 00:13:02,715
[Espen] You're not real. The sea left.

110
00:13:42,665 --> 00:13:44,335
[Espen] ...minute six.

111
00:13:47,665 --> 00:13:50,325
[Espen] Behind the lens. One spare. Dry.

112
00:14:02,165 --> 00:14:04,555
[Espen] For the night the tin lies.

113
00:14:14,165 --> 00:14:15,765
[Espen] Burn.

114
00:14:52,665 --> 00:14:56,315
[Espen] Six down. Six up. That's the whole song, isn't it.

115
00:15:00,165 --> 00:15:02,715
[Orla] Kettle... had further to fall.

116
00:15:04,165 --> 00:15:07,815
[Espen] Don't joke. You're not allowed to joke on a floor.

117
00:15:33,165 --> 00:15:36,375
[Orla] Your grandfather kept weather in jars too.

118
00:15:38,165 --> 00:15:41,315
[Orla] He never believed it either. Then he did.

119
00:15:42,665 --> 00:15:45,875
[Espen] Gran. The thing at the glass. Its eye was—

120
00:15:47,665 --> 00:15:49,265
[Espen] Gran?

121
00:15:52,665 --> 00:15:55,325
[Espen] Fine. Sleep. I've got the count.

122
00:16:52,865 --> 00:16:54,465
[Orla] Seven.

123
00:16:56,465 --> 00:16:58,405
[Espen] Eight. One snapped.

124
00:17:00,865 --> 00:17:02,595
[Orla] Snapped counts.

125
00:17:08,865 --> 00:17:10,975
[Espen] I'll buy more matches.

126
00:17:12,865 --> 00:17:14,475
[Orla] Buy two tins.

127
00:17:16,465 --> 00:17:18,685
[Espen] And putty. For the pane.

128
00:17:19,265 --> 00:17:20,865
[Orla] I know.

129
00:17:27,815 --> 00:17:31,025
<i>[dozens of small bells, far below, rising]</i>

130
00:17:40,215 --> 00:17:41,815
[Espen] Hulda.

131
00:17:42,135 --> 00:17:45,615
[Hulda] It's dawn, boy. Dawn is for bakers and regrets.

132
00:17:47,515 --> 00:17:49,115
[Hulda] What's this?

133
00:17:49,295 --> 00:17:52,565
[Espen] Change. From yesterday. Your scale was off.

134
00:17:53,160 --> 00:17:55,270
[Hulda] My scale is never off.

135
00:17:55,660 --> 00:17:57,260
[Espen] Then I was.

136
00:17:58,160 --> 00:18:01,430
[Espen] What does a month of oil cost? Full weight.

137
00:18:01,610 --> 00:18:03,940
[Hulda] More than a bicycle wheel.

138
00:18:04,535 --> 00:18:06,365
[Espen] Two months, then.

139
00:18:06,835 --> 00:18:08,725
[Hulda] Storm keep you up?

140
00:18:09,235 --> 00:18:10,905
[Espen] Something did.

141
00:18:22,335 --> 00:18:26,095
[Bellfarer] Saltwick Light. Still burning past dawn. Good habit.

142
00:18:26,275 --> 00:18:30,525
[Bellfarer] Three weeks on the flats, out of Farholm. My bells are tired.

143
00:18:31,130 --> 00:18:32,730
[Espen] Why bells?

144
00:18:37,230 --> 00:18:40,330
[Bellfarer] So the dark can hear I'm not part of it.

145
00:18:41,630 --> 00:18:46,270
[Bellfarer] Cut this from Farholm's keeper-door. Cold as a drowned man's pocket.

146
00:18:46,450 --> 00:18:49,660
[Bellfarer] Last night the tide rose past my hat brim.

147
00:18:50,760 --> 00:18:53,360
[Bellfarer] Where a light forgets its keep,

148
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:56,670
[Bellfarer] the old sea rises from its sleep.

149
00:18:57,760 --> 00:19:00,750
[Hulda] Farholm's dark? I thought it was haze.

150
00:19:00,930 --> 00:19:02,820
[Bellfarer] It was never haze.

151
00:19:03,720 --> 00:19:08,300
[Bellfarer] Three weeks. Nothing has come down off that cliff. Nothing I heard.

152
00:19:11,620 --> 00:19:13,560
[Bellfarer] Who keeps this one?

153
00:19:18,420 --> 00:19:20,020
[Espen] I do.

154
00:20:08,420 --> 00:20:11,570
<i>The law says every light burns till dawn.</i>

155
00:20:13,420 --> 00:20:15,250
<i>Now you know why.</i>
